{"title":"Career Roadmap · Primary Teacher (PRT)","role":"Primary Teacher (PRT)","summary":"A Primary Teacher (PRT) teaches young learners at the foundational and primary-school levels. The role focuses on building strong foundations in:","facts":{"Current degree":"Other Teacher Education (D.El.Ed / B.El.Ed / B.P.Ed / ITEP / Integrated B.Sc-B.Ed / BA-B.Ed)","Course":"Elementary Education (D.El.Ed / B.El.Ed)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Primary Teacher (PRT) teaches young learners at the foundational and primary-school levels. The role focuses on building strong foundations in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literacy"},{"text":"Numeracy"},{"text":"Environmental awareness"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Social and emotional development"},{"text":"Creativity"},{"text":"Learning habits"},{"text":"Basic digital literacy"},{"text":"Primary teachers need to understand how children learn, not just what they need to learn."}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Planning age-appropriate lessons"},{"text":"Teaching foundational subjects"},{"text":"Classroom management"},{"text":"Continuous assessment"},{"text":"Remedial teaching"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Student observation"},{"text":"Inclusive education"},{"text":"Co-curricular activities"},{"text":"Maintaining academic records"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"PRT eligibility varies by recruiting authority and school system. D.El.Ed/B.El.Ed, TET qualification, language requirements, age limits and other conditions can differ. Candidates should always verify the current official recruitment notification for the specific state, central-school system or employer. A teaching qualification alone does not guarantee appointment."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","D.El.Ed / B.El.E